; Print a name with its article, then "is" or "are"
;
; Message control codes 17 (after #R$7425 loads the first object) and 19
; (#R$742D takes the id from the stack). Like #R$740C, but PhraseMode is set to
; 1, so the name is printed with its article (#R$7478 calls #R$743F). The id
; goes to A', the shared tail #R$7411 prints the name and returns the word for
; "are" (the player) or "is" (anyone else).
; .
; The printer calls this handler with IX at the code byte; NZ with a word code
; in DE means print that word.
;
; A Id of the thing named (PLAYER prints "you", $FF "someone")
; O:DE Word code: "is" ($039B) or "are" ($0065)
; O:F NZ
@label=PrintNameIs
c$7428 EX AF,AF'     ; id of the thing to A'
 $7429 LD A,$01      ; PhraseMode 1: print with an article
 $742B JR $7411      ; #R$7411 stores PhraseMode, prints the name
